### Analysis & Design
Define public API: constrctor(maxRequests: number, windowMs: number), allowRequest(now?: number): boolean.

Key design decisions:
1. Maintain immutable timestamps array during filtering.
2. Precise wall-clock time propagation required for robust rate limiting.
3. Implement strict black-box testing w/o inspecting internal mutable state.

### Implementation
```typescript
export class TSRateLimiter {
  private readonly maxRequests: number;
  private readonly windowMs: number;
  private timestamps: number[] = [];

  constructor(maxRequests: number, windowMs: number) {
    if (maxRequests <= 0 || windowMs <= 0) throw new Error('Parameters must be positive');
    this.maxRequests = maxRequests;
    this.windowMs = windowMs;
  }

  allowRequest(now = Date.now()): boolean {
    const cutoff = now - this.windowMs;
    this.timestamps = this.timestamps.filter(ts => ts <= cutoff);

    if (this.timestamps.length < this.maxRequests) {
      this.timestamps.push(now);
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
